LESSON 9: ORDER AND COUNTING

⍋V IS GRADE UP: NOT THE SORTED VECTOR, BUT THE POSITIONS
THAT WOULD SORT IT. INDEXING BY IT DOES THE SORTING. TRY:

      ⍋3 1 2
      V←31 4 15 9
      V[⍋V]
      V[⍒V]

⍒ IS GRADE DOWN. THE GRADE IS MORE USEFUL THAN A SORT: IT
CAN ORDER A SECOND VECTOR THE SAME WAY, NAMES BY SCORES.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      V←31 4 15 9
⎕:
      V[⍋V]
4 9 15 31
⎕:
      GO
?N IS A NUMBER FROM 1 TO N, DIFFERENT EACH TIME, AND M?N IS
M DIFFERENT ONES: A ROLL, AND A DEAL. TRY:

      ?6
      ?6 6
      5?10

THE SEQUENCE STARTS FROM THE SAME PLACE IN EVERY CLEAR
WORKSPACE, SO A PROGRAM USING ? CAN BE RUN AGAIN EXACTLY.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      ?6 6
1 5
⎕:
      5?10
5 6 4 3 9
