LESSON 10: CHARACTERS

CHARACTERS GO IN QUOTES, AND A ROW OF THEM IS A VECTOR LIKE
ANY OTHER. A QUOTE INSIDE IS DOUBLED. TRY:

      'HELLO'
      ⍴'HELLO'
      'IT''S'
      'ABC','DEF'

'A' IS A SINGLE CHARACTER, A SCALAR, AND ⍴'A' IS EMPTY AS
⍴7 WAS; ,'A' IS A VECTOR OF ONE.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      'IT''S'
IT'S
⎕:
      GO
COMPARISON, MEMBERSHIP, INDEX-OF, COMPRESSION AND REVERSAL
ALL WORK ON CHARACTERS. TRY:

      'HELLO'='L'
      'HELLO'⍳'L'
      'HELLO'∊'AEIOU'
      (~'HELLO'∊'AEIOU')/'HELLO'
      ⌽'HELLO'

THE FOURTH KEEPS THE CONSONANTS: THE VOWELS ARE FOUND BY
MEMBERSHIP, NEGATED, AND USED TO COMPRESS.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      (~'HELLO'∊'AEIOU')/'HELLO'
HLL
⎕:
      GO
A MATRIX OF CHARACTERS IS A LIST OF WORDS, ONE TO A ROW,
